**Scot, Scots(wo)man, Scotch(wo)man.** Englishmen use the third forms by nature, the first sometimes for brevity or for poetical or rhetorical or jocular effect, & the second occasionally in compliment to a Scotch hearer, *Scots-* being (OED)
